<title>USA: US Treasury 2-yr note sale seen yielding 6.16 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 2-yr note sale seen yielding 6.16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $18.75 billion in two-year notes is expected to produce an average yield near 6.16/6.165 percent Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1235 EDT/1635 GMT, the two-year notes were quoted at 6.16 percent in when-issued trade.</p>
<p>Dealers said they expected good demand for the notes.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue will be well bid,&quot; said one trader. &quot;There's some good foreign buying, but the domestic books are mixed. I think it'll come in pretty close to these (current) levels.&quot;</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1661</p>
